  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "How do I submit a design request?",
      "expanded": "How do I submit a design request?\n\nYou and your team can request design work through a shared board we will set up for you in Asana. You can request as many designs as you like."
    },
    {
      "question": "How does onboarding work?",
      "expanded": "How does onboarding work?\n\nYour account manager will set up a call to discuss your design needs. After that, you’ll receive an invitation to your design board on Asana, along with instructions on how to add your design requests"
    },
    {
      "question": "How fast will I receive my designs?",
      "expanded": "How fast will I receive my designs?\n\nYou can set your own deadlines for designs but on average, we deliver a design within a couple of days."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do you work at our company?",
      "expanded": "Do you work at our company?\n\nIt may feel like it but we do not work at your company however we do stay in close touch to make sure we provide the best service possible."
    },
    {
      "question": "Why not hire full-time?",
      "expanded": "Why not hire full-time?\n\nA full-time designer can be expensive and hard to source. Your company may not have enough work to keep a full-time designer busy."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I order a one-time logo service?",
      "expanded": "Can I order a one-time logo service?\n\nWe offer a combined All-In-One plan to help you with all your design needs. You’re welcome to upgrade for one month to get the designs you need, then return to your previous plan for the following month."
    },
    {
      "question": "What tools do you use?",
      "expanded": "What tools do you use?\n\nWe work in a wide range of design software, including Figma, Photoshop, Illustrator, After Effects, Canva, and many others."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is your refund policy?",
      "expanded": "What is your refund policy?\n\nBecause we deliver custom design work it’s not possible to issue a refund."
    }
  ],
